\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.1}{\ignorespaces Per-class Banking77 error concentration for the native query head. Left: Lorenz curve of the 338{} errors, with Jev's 234{} errors beside it. Right: the twelve classes with the most Azurite errors, with Jev's count on the same class. The largest single class, \texttt {pending\_transfer}, accounts for 12{} of the 338{} errors; 70{} of 77 classes have at least one. The boundary is broad, not concentrated in a few intents. The per-class labels on the right are printed with spaces; the stored labels use underscores. Values are recomputed from the per-example records by \texttt {thesis/gen\_figures.py}.\relax }}{40}{figure.caption.27}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.2}{\ignorespaces Accuracy of the mean-pool and message-query heads at three context settings. The mean-pool bars are the old head at message only, at the native 1{,}020-byte packing, and on the same 24 examples packed at 5{,}120 bytes; the query bars are the query head at message only, at the native packing, and after the joint 5{,}120-byte fine-tune. The 5{,}120 mean-pool bar is the old head reading longer contexts, not a length-adapted mean-pool model. The dashed line is Jev's 92.40\% on the same 3{,}080 rows. Values are recomputed from the stored per-example files by \texttt {thesis/gen\_figures.py}.\relax }}{43}{figure.caption.30}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.3}{\ignorespaces Query-head accuracy against mean context length. The three points are message-only (0 examples), the native complete-example packing (11.9{} examples on average), and the joint 5{,}120-byte fine-tune (24 examples). The dashed line is Jev's 92.40\%; the diamond marks the reconstructed median Jev prompt, 10{,}683{} bytes, of which 7{,}801{} bytes are the 77 category definitions. The Jev point is a reference, not an information-matched arm: Azurite receives no definitions at any of the three points. Values are recomputed from the stored summaries and per-example files by \texttt {thesis/gen\_figures.py}.\relax }}{44}{figure.caption.31}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.4}{\ignorespaces Train/test separation for the joint 5{,}120-byte fine-tune. The bars show 96.62\% on the 4{,}000 training rows (3{,}865/4{,}000) and 87.11\% on the 3{,}080 official test rows (2{,}683/3{,}080), with 95\% Wilson intervals. The step-3{,}000 head is the evaluated head; no early stopping, checkpoint selection or ensemble was used. The dashed line is Jev's 92.40\%. The test--train gap is 9.51{} points. The vertical axis begins at 80\%. Values are recomputed from the stored summary by \texttt {thesis/gen\_figures.py}.\relax }}{45}{figure.caption.32}%
